🔐 Linux Admin Tip – Safely Edit Critical System Files

Want to edit /etc/passwd, /etc/shadow, /etc/group, or /etc/gshadow the right way?

✅ Use these safe commands to prevent file corruption:

vipw – edit /etc/passwd

vigr – edit /etc/group

vipw -s – edit /etc/shadow

vigr -s – edit /etc/gshadow


📌 These commands lock the file while editing to avoid race conditions or corruption.
